{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:2b2740cdf152a7f5","name":"Outlaw","source":{"id":"source:reference-2b2740cdf152a7f5","title":"Outlaw","revision":25265,"timestamp":"2024-11-13T20:30:04Z","sha256":"3268fe38a656f086f87ec5299eb56f214b02c5df1f7dfafbf9155262865bff0b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=25265","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Outlaw&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-2b2740cdf152a7f5","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Scum and Villainy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scum_and_Villainy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Where there is law, there are those who would break it, circumvent it, and fly in its face. Outlaws are rogue individuals who rightly or wrongly have crossed the line and now pay the price for their indiscretion. Naturally, Outlaws cover a lot of territory, from freedom fighters waging a private war against tyranny to bloodthirsty cutthroats and murderers wanted in twelve systems.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Outlaws can include a whole host of characters, but the most notorious Outlaws are those who make being outside the law their primary profession. Their exploits are the stuff of legend, bucking authority and causing so much trouble that arrest warrants have been issued.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Outlaws sometimes earn respect from common citizens of the galaxy. Regardless of the crimes they commit to earn their outlaw status, their ability to evade capture resonates with those who have suffered from oppression. In some systems, Outlaws can even get supplies, shelter, and support from common folk, and if they help these people, they might be seen as true heroes.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Examples of Outlaws in Star Wars:"]}," Cornelius Evazan, Fenn Shysa, Joilli, Ponda Baba, Scoryn.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Prerequisites:"]}," To qualify to become an Outlaw, a character must fulfill the following criteria:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Minimum Level:"]}," 7th"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Trained Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Trained_Skills"},":"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Survival"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Survival","referenceId":"reference:8302496de0ace160"}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Talent"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Talent"},":"]}," Any one Talent from either the\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Disgrace Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Disgrace_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:934cf1fece146b2a"}," or"]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Misfortune Talent Tree"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Misfortune_Talent_Tree","referenceId":"reference:572da85689e76d52"}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," You must be wanted by the authorities in at least one star system"]}]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Game Rule Information"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Outlaws have the following game statistics: \n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["BASE ATTACK BONUS"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/BASE_ATTACK_BONUS"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CLASS FEATURES\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["\n"],"rowspan":6},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["BASE ATTACK BONUS"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/BASE_ATTACK_BONUS"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th